## Purpose

This single file defines backend work in numbered parts. Each part records the existing modules to reuse, candidate new file paths, required integration, dependencies, tests and acceptance criteria. It is an implementation structure, not a claim that the proposed files have already been created or that HOMIO is production-ready.

## Status vocabulary

- **EXISTING — INSPECTED:** Path was found and its relevant purpose/source was inspected.
- **EXISTING — INTEGRATION UNVERIFIED:** Domain code exists, but production persistence/API wiring/deployment or end-to-end behavior is not proven.
- **PROPOSED ADD:** Candidate new path. Confirm the approved architecture, search for equivalents and check dependencies before creating it.
- **UPDATE / CONNECT:** Extend or wire existing canonical code. Do not create a competing domain engine.
- **BLOCKED BY DESIGN:** Confirm the approved architecture/technology lock before selecting a database, queue, provider, runtime or new source of truth.
- **PASS:** Use only when an actual targeted test/runtime check succeeds against a named commit and evidence is recorded.

## Non-negotiable authority and safety rules

1. `REOS_CONTROL_CENTER/data/state.json` remains the machine-readable execution/gate authority.
2. Branch `reos-development` remains the canonical code/history source.
3. The approved master architecture and ARCH-037/ARCH-038 schema/technology decisions govern implementation. Do not guess a stack.
4. One business source of truth per domain. Search indexes, caches, analytics, AI summaries and ACRL reconstruction are not canonical business state.
5. Do not create duplicate identity, tenant, inventory, lead-ownership, event, deal, trust/fraud, commission, governance, Control Center or ACRL engines.
6. ACRL owns continuity, reconstruction, checkpoints and recovery—not live customer, inventory, lead, deal or commission domain truth.
7. File existence, compile success, UI rendering, or an unrelated green CI run is not proof of feature completion.
8. Never commit real credentials, tokens, signing secrets or customer personal data.
9. Before every repository change, reread live HEAD and target blob SHA; use the guarded remote-write process defined by the repository, fail closed on mismatch, and read back the resulting commit and file.
10. This document cannot silently change the current Control Center gate or mark an acceptance criterion complete.

