### Required behavior

1. Validate provider signature, exact issuer, audience, expiry and required claims; protect state, nonce and PKCE.
2. Resolve exact `(issuer, sub)` to a durable canonical REOS identity.
3. Do not auto-link accounts by email alone.
4. Reject disabled/suspended identities and inactive, revoked or expired memberships.
5. Establish tenant context and capabilities server-side; do not trust client-supplied role/tenant values.
6. Enforce authorization on every protected operation and every returned resource, including search, documents, saved properties, visits, leads, deals and commissions.
7. Implement durable server-side session revocation/expiry according to the approved architecture.
8. Protect state-changing browser actions against CSRF/origin abuse; use secure cookie controls, rate limiting and privacy-safe logging.
9. Do not return raw provider errors, tokens, credentials or private claims to clients.
10. Keep authentication separate from authorization.

### Required negative/positive tests

Valid and invalid tokens; invalid signature; issuer/audience mismatch; expired token; missing claims; callback state/nonce/PKCE failure; unknown external identity; disabled account; expired/revoked membership; revoked session; no tenant context; tenant mismatch; resource IDOR; missing capability; logout/revocation behavior.

### Acceptance criteria

OIDC login alone cannot grant tenant or privileged access. Account resolution, membership lookup, access denial and session revocation are supported by end-to-end evidence.

